22.7 Why Is It Thread-Safe?

Because synchronization provides:

Mutual Exclusion
Only one thread enters the critical section.

Atomicity
Although

count++;
is internally

Read
↓
Modify
↓
Write

the entire sequence executes while holding the monitor.
No other thread can interleave these steps.

Visibility

When a thread exits a synchronized block:
Changes are flushed to main memory.

When another thread enters:
It sees the latest values.

This is guaranteed by the Java Memory Model (JMM).


